# Supabase — Project Settings → API
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=your-service-role-key
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# Google AI Studio — https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Task A (vision/food-photo scanning) primary — single key, no multi-key pool.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key

# --- Task-based AI routing: non-Gemini providers ---------------------------
# Each key is independently optional (a blank one just drops that provider
# out of its task's fallback chain — see CLAUDE.md's "Task-based AI routing"
# section) but MISTRAL_API_KEY is the practical minimum: without it (and
# without GROQ_API_KEY too), every Task B/C feature (macro re-estimation,
# meal suggestions, coach chat/recap/damage-control) falls straight to the
# native-Gemini last resort (GEMINI_TEXT_MODELS below) on every single call,
# not just when genuinely needed. All three are OpenAI-compatible endpoints
# called via openai.AsyncOpenAI.
#
# Cerebras and Chutes were tried here too and removed — both required
# funding a billing balance to serve any request at all (a 402 on every
# call while unfunded), which defeats the point of a free fallback tier.
# The native-Gemini fallback (GEMINI_TEXT_MODELS below) replaced their role.

# Task A vision fallback (only reached if Gemini's whole model chain fails) —
# https://build.nvidia.com. Comma-separated, tried in order on a retryable
# error. z-ai/glm-5.2 (the old default) reached end-of-life 2026-08-21 (live
# 410 Gone) — replaced with nvidia/nemotron-nano-12b-v2-vl and
# meta/llama-3.2-11b-vision-instruct, both live-verified with a real image
# request. meta/llama-3.2-90b-vision-instruct was tried too and timed out
# (40s+, likely cold-start) — deliberately excluded. Re-verify this list's
# own account catalog (GET /v1/models) periodically; NIM models get
# end-of-life'd with little notice.
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=your-nvidia-api-key
# NVIDIA_VISION_MODELS=nvidia/nemotron-nano-12b-v2-vl,meta/llama-3.2-11b-vision-instruct

# Task B/C primary — https://console.mistral.ai/api-keys. Promoted ahead of
# Groq (2026-08) for stricter JSON-mode adherence and no hidden-reasoning-
# token cost on multi-ingredient descriptions — see CLAUDE.md's "Task-based
# AI routing" section. MISTRAL_MODELS is ONE shared catalog for both Task B
# (macro/ingredient extraction, accuracy-first) and Task C (chat/recap,
# throughput-first) — gemini_service.py applies two different priority
# orderings over this same list/quota pool rather than splitting it into two
# settings (see that file's _MISTRAL_ACCURACY_PRIORITY/_MISTRAL_CHAT_PRIORITY
# and config.py's mistral_models comment for why). RPM figures were read
# directly off this account's live x-ratelimit-limit-req-minute response
# headers; there is no daily-limit header, so RPD below is a conservative,
# safe-to-loosen placeholder, not a verified number.
MISTRAL_API_KEY=your-mistral-api-key
# mistral-large-* is paid-tier-only (403 tier_not_allowed on the free tier as of 2026-08) — omitted; ids are pinned/dated, not "-latest". See config.py's mistral_models comment.
# MISTRAL_MODELS=mistral-medium-3.5:50:20000,mistral-small-2603:50:20000,ministral-8b-2512:188:100000,ministral-3b-2512:750:400000
# MISTRAL_MODEL_RPM=30
# MISTRAL_MODEL_RPD=1000

# Task B/C first fallback (only reached once Mistral's whole model chain
# fails/is exhausted) — https://console.groq.com/keys. GROQ_MODELS is an
# ordered, comma-separated candidate list just like GEMINI_MODELS below
# (same "name" or "name:rpm:rpd" format, same quota-aware cycling via
# services/quota_service.py — the mechanism is fully generic across
# providers now). Verified against console.groq.com/docs/rate-limits: the
# first four models are all ~30 RPM/1,000 RPD at comparable quality (trying
# all four roughly 4x's the daily ceiling at full quality before ever
# leaving Groq); llama-3.1-8b-instant is meaningfully weaker but gets 30
# RPM/14,400 RPD, so it's kept LAST as a high-volume safety valve once the
# quality tier is genuinely exhausted, not a default choice.
GROQ_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key
# GROQ_MODELS=llama-3.3-70b-versatile:30:1000,openai/gpt-oss-120b:30:1000,qwen/qwen3.6-27b:30:1000,openai/gpt-oss-20b:30:1000,llama-3.1-8b-instant:30:14400
# GROQ_MODEL_RPM=30
# GROQ_MODEL_RPD=1000

# Smart Gemini model routing (Task A only): ordered candidate list. Each entry is a bare model
# name (uses GEMINI_MODEL_RPM/RPD below) or "name:rpm:rpd" for its own limit
# — free-tier quotas vary a lot by model (check `api_limits`, repo root, and
# Google AI Studio for this project's real numbers). The backend routes to
# whichever candidate has headroom before each call, falling back through
# the rest on a live error — but only through models that actually exist for
# your project; a 404'd/retired model name left in this list wastes a
# round-trip if it's mid-list, and can surface as a real user-facing error if
# it's the LAST entry and every earlier candidate's RPM happens to be dry at
# the same moment. Default is tiered by quota and accuracy: two big-quota
# Flash-Lite models carry real traffic (each its own pool, so two roughly
# doubles daily capacity), two regular Flash variants absorb overflow at
# smaller quota but better accuracy. Buying paid-tier credits later is just
# editing this list — verify each model name in Google AI Studio first.
# GEMINI_MODELS=gemini-flash-lite-latest:12:480,gemini-3.1-flash-lite:12:480,gemini-3.6-flash:4:18,gemini-3.5-flash:4:18

# Fallback RPM/RPD for any bare (no ":rpm:rpd") entry in GEMINI_MODELS above.
# GEMINI_MODEL_RPM=12
# GEMINI_MODEL_RPD=480

# Thinking budget for the no-photo "describe what I ate" path (POST
# /scan/describe) — inferring composition + portion from free text needs real
# reasoning, so this isn't 0 like the simple food-name lookup, but there's no
# image to reason over either, so it's set lower than GEMINI_VISION_THINKING_BUDGET.
# GEMINI_DESCRIPTION_THINKING_BUDGET=512

# Task B/C's TRUE last-resort fallback — only reached once Groq's entire
# model chain has failed. Uses Gemini's native SDK
# (not the OpenAI-compat shim, which can't disable "thinking" on any model
# this account can reach — see CLAUDE.md's "Task-based AI routing"
# section). Deliberately a DIFFERENT model than GEMINI_MODELS above, so
# this draws from a separate quota pool and never competes with Task A's
# vision traffic. 5 RPM is confirmed straight from a live 429's own error
# body; the RPD figure is an unverified conservative placeholder — safe to
# loosen, since a wrong number here only ever costs one wasted round-trip.
# GEMINI_TEXT_MODELS=gemini-3-flash-preview:5:100
# GEMINI_TEXT_MODEL_RPM=5
# GEMINI_TEXT_MODEL_RPD=100

# Composite-dish "chef": a dedicated high-tier NATIVE Gemini model used ONLY
# for a composite/cooked prepared dish's whole-dish AI estimate (the
# skip_database=True path). The cheap Task B chain under-estimates these (drops
# cooking fat, mis-composes regional recipes — verified by live A/B test).
# DISABLED by default (blank) — no high-tier Gemini model is available on a
# free-tier key (Pro models are paid-only / retired; see config.py's
# gemini_composite_models comment). Enable only with a paid Google AI plan:
# GEMINI_COMPOSITE_MODELS=gemini-3.1-pro-preview:5:100
# GEMINI_COMPOSITE_MODEL_RPM=5
# GEMINI_COMPOSITE_MODEL_RPD=100
# GEMINI_COMPOSITE_THINKING_BUDGET=2048

# ============================================================================
# Web Push notifications — standards-based VAPID push, no Firebase/OneSignal.
# Optional: both blank means push is simply off (routers/notifications.py's
# endpoints 503 cleanly instead of crashing). Requires an always-on process
# to actually deliver in the background (see CLAUDE.md's Web Push section) —
# viable now that this runs on a 24/7 VPS rather than a scale-to-zero host.
# ============================================================================

# Generate a keypair once with (see backend/config.py's own comment for the
# exact command — py_vapid ships no ready-made "print me a keypair" helper):
#   python3 -c "
#   from cryptography.hazmat.primitives import serialization
#   from py_vapid import Vapid02
#   from py_vapid.utils import b64urlencode
#   v = Vapid02(); v.generate_keys()
#   priv = v.private_key.private_numbers().private_value.to_bytes(32, 'big')
#   pub = v.public_key.public_bytes(serialization.Encoding.X962, serialization.PublicFormat.UncompressedPoint)
#   print('VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=' + b64urlencode(pub))
#   print('VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=' + b64urlencode(priv))
#   "
# The public key also needs to be copied into frontend/js/config.js's
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY — it's not secret (shipped to every browser), only the
# private key needs protecting.
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=

# The `sub` claim every push service requires in the VAPID JWT (RFC 8292) —
# a contact URI so a push service operator can reach you if this server ever
# misbehaves. Must be "mailto:" + a real address you read, not a placeholder.
# VAPID_ADMIN_EMAIL=mailto:you@example.com

# Comma-separated list of origins allowed to call this API
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,https://your-username.github.io

# How many days of daily_logs/water_logs to keep before they're purged
# (rolling window, not calendar weeks). weight_logs is never purged — see
# sql/schema.sql. Keep this in sync with the interval in cleanup_old_logs().
# RETENTION_DAYS=7

# Optional: free Sentry project DSN (sentry.io) for backend error tracking.
# Leave blank to disable entirely — nothing else changes.
# SENTRY_DSN=

# Nutrition database grounding (services/nutrition_db_service.py) — before
# trusting the AI's own recalled macros for an identified food, this looks
# it up against USDA FoodData Central and Open Food Facts, using the
# database's real values on a confident text match instead. Open Food Facts
# needs no key and works with everything below left blank; USDA needs its
# own free key for full coverage of generic/raw ingredients — get one
# instantly (no approval wait) at https://api.data.gov/signup. DEMO_KEY
# works for local testing but is rate-limited hard (30/hour) — never use it
# in production, a real key is free and instant.
# USDA_API_KEY=your-usda-api-key
# Kill switch — set to false to instantly revert to pure-AI estimation
# (skips both database sources entirely) without a code rollback.
# NUTRITION_DB_GROUNDING_ENABLED=true

# Note: Turnstile (CAPTCHA on signup) has no backend env var — it's
# configured entirely in the Supabase dashboard (Authentication → Attack
# Protection), with its own secret key that never touches this backend. See
# frontend/js/config.js for the public site key the frontend needs.
